Consider an RDFGraph UniKG and another node table Students and a rel table SameAs from Students to UniKG_r. You can drop UniKG even if that would leave Students around. Normally this would give a Binder exception that says: "Cannot delete node table nodeTableX referenced by rel table relTableY." 

To replicate:
```
kuzu> CREATE RDF Graph UniKG;
kuzu> CREATE NODE TABLE Students(name STRING, primary key (name));
kuzu> CREATE REL TABLE SameStudent(FROM Students TO UniKG_r);
kuzu> DROP TABLE UniKG;
kuzu>  MATCH (a:Students)-[s:SameStudent]->(b) RETURN *;
Error: unordered_map::at: key not found
```
Normally, this would happen:
```
kuzu> CREATE NODE TABLE nodeTable1 (name STRING, primary key (name));
kuzu> CREATE NODE TABLE nodeTable2 (name STRING, primary key (name));
kuzu> CREATE REL TABLE relTable (FROM nodeTable1 TO nodeTable2);
kuzu> DROP TABLE nodeTable2;
Error: Binder exception: Cannot delete node table nodeTable2 referenced by rel table relTable.
```
So the system does not allow dropping nodeTable2.

## Overview
In the `SignExtend` function in `src/include/storage/compression/sign_extend.h`, when the provided parameter `width` is equal to the size of `T_U`, the bitshift `(T_U(1) << width)` will overflow and (at least on clang 17.0.1) the value will be zeroed out instead extracting its `width` lowest bits.

## Steps to reproduce
I've created a case that causes the SignExtend function to fail [here](https://godbolt.org/z/TPM8KrYrY) as well as a potential fix.

I haven't tried this directly but the adding the following case to `test/storage/compression_test.cpp` should also reproduce the error (bitpacking where the bitWidth is the same as the original size of the element to pack):

```
TEST(CompressionTests, IntegerPackingTest8Small) {
    auto length = 3;
    std::vector<int8_t> src(length, 0);
    src[0] = 0;
    src[1] = -127;
    src[2] = 128;
    auto alg = IntegerBitpacking<int8_t>();
    test_compression(alg, src);
}
```

## Expected behaviour:
The above test case should pass, and `SignExtend` should return the correct sign-extended value (and not 0) even when `width == sizeof(T_U)`

